  "DAL PRIV": {
    "_comment": "Split out of the pooled DFW-DAL page on 2026-10-20 (Sam). While pooled, DAL's launch was gated per-dist via DFW-DAL's labor_from_first_debrief, because a station-wide gate there would have erased every DFW hour before DAL's first JSX debrief. Standing alone it takes the ordinary station gate instead. EXPECT THIS PAGE TO READ OVER: 7 JSX debrief rows of budget against one salaried head imputed at 5.71 h/day, with no hourly punches since the gate date. That is a staffing picture, not an over-run.",
    "hours_from_first_debrief": true
  },
  "CLE DAY": {
    "_comment": "CLE's one labor dist (CLE AA) is split into two crews by punch-in clock hour. DAY takes punches starting 07:00-18:59 local and carries no salaried imputation - the single CLE AA salaried head is assigned to NIGHT. Day shifts get plain calendar-day attribution (a 7 AM start belongs to that day, not the previous one). Budget is the facility share on the CLE DAY sheet; all Ultra and Frontier work belongs to NIGHT."
  },
  "CLE NIGHT": {
    "_comment": "NIGHT takes CLE AA punches starting 19:00-06:59 local plus ALL CLE AA salaried time. The window wraps midnight, so it keeps the punch-in-minus-12h attribution that groups an overnight shift onto the day it started. Carries the Ultra, Shroud and Frontier work plus its share of the facility budget.",
